  "story": "Human herders became a way of life among the humans ~8 kyr ago where its ways suited the land better than its people's, on the continent at 76\u00b0S 99\u00b0W (68 Mkm\u00b2). ~2.6 kyr ago it walked over a land bridge (low sea) to the continent at 18\u00b0N 43\u00b0E (28 Mkm\u00b2). ~1.5 kyr ago it walked over a land bridge (low sea) to the island at 17\u00b0N 170\u00b0W (0.084 Mkm\u00b2). ~400 years ago it walked over a land bridge (low sea) to the continent at 49\u00b0S 2\u00b0E (24 Mkm\u00b2). Today: 21 million in 22.27 Mkm\u00b2 in 101 separate lands (the largest 21%); neighbours human farmers, humans, human nomads, genasi (elemental). The human herders hold 16% of the world's best pasture (10 Mkm\u00b2, the heart of it in the country at 36\u00b0N 15\u00b0E); and they hold 14% of the world's best farmland (6.7 Mkm\u00b2, the heart of it in the country at 41\u00b0S 80\u00b0W). It was the first to tame the horse, ~6 kyr ago on the open grassland of the continent at 76\u00b0S 99\u00b0W (68 Mkm\u00b2). It took up dogs (~2.3 kyr ago), sheep and goats (~8 kyr ago) and cattle (~6.2 kyr ago). Its milk-drinking 60% keep dairy herds of cattle and horses and sheep and goats. The human herders 60% digest milk as adults. It cooks over dung fires.",
